1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,892
Every large AI training run has a hidden tax.

2
00:00:04,442 --> 00:00:08,306
This video is about what it costs you — and how to stop paying it.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,536
Every twenty to thirty minutes, a training job stops to save a checkpoint — the model's weights, and its optimizer state.

4
00:00:18,036 --> 00:00:21,252
While that file writes, your GPUs do nothing.

5
00:00:21,852 --> 00:00:28,044
At H100 rates, one large checkpoint can burn about five dollars of idle GPU time.

6
00:00:28,494 --> 00:00:33,030
Now multiply that by every checkpoint, every node, every day.

7
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:36,476
So why does this happen?

8
00:00:36,926 --> 00:00:46,526
Checkpoints are big — ten to a hundred-plus gibibytes — and they're written to durable, shared storage, like NFS or Azure NetApp Files.

9
00:00:47,026 --> 00:00:51,250
Durable storage is the right place for them. It survives crashes.

10
00:00:51,750 --> 00:00:56,022
But it's slow — and that write sits on the training loop's critical path.

11
00:00:56,522 --> 00:00:59,234
The bigger the checkpoint, the longer the stall.

12
00:00:59,684 --> 00:01:07,628
At 128 gigabytes, the durable path can hold your GPUs for two and a half minutes — every single time.

13
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:14,772
AIFS — the AI File System Accelerator — fixes this with one idea:

14
00:01:15,172 --> 00:01:17,956
decouple performance from durability.

15
00:01:18,556 --> 00:01:25,660
AIFS is a filesystem layer. Your training job just writes to a normal directory — no code changes.

16
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:32,832
Behind the mount, writes land on fast local NVMe first — and training resumes immediately.

17
00:01:33,332 --> 00:01:40,004
In the background, AIFS replicates the data to your durable storage — which stays the source of truth.

18
00:01:40,504 --> 00:01:49,600
And when every file in a checkpoint is safely replicated, AIFS writes a commit marker: this checkpoint is complete, and trustworthy.

19
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:53,384
Now — let's watch it actually work.

20
00:01:53,884 --> 00:01:59,284
This is the real prototype — open source, written in C — running live.

21
00:01:59,834 --> 00:02:05,354
On the left: the local NVMe spool. On the right: the durable backend.

22
00:02:05,954 --> 00:02:11,570
We save a multi-file training checkpoint — model, optimizer, scheduler state.

23
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:18,144
Watch the left side. The files appear instantly — the training job is already unblocked.

24
00:02:18,844 --> 00:02:25,396
Now the right side. The same files arrive one by one, as the background replicator copies them over.

25
00:02:26,096 --> 00:02:32,360
And last of all, the commit marker — .aifs_committed — appears, sealing the checkpoint.

26
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:41,168
If the node crashed mid-copy, that marker would never be written — and training would simply resume from the previous committed checkpoint.

27
00:02:41,668 --> 00:02:43,900
Durability — without the wait.

28
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:55,100
On real Azure hardware with local NVMe, the prototype sustains 879 megabytes per second — on the fully durable path.

29
00:02:55,650 --> 00:03:00,282
A four-gibibyte checkpoint is locally safe in under five seconds.

30
00:03:00,732 --> 00:03:05,412
Replication finishes about half a minute later — off the critical path.

31
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:09,980
And that speed converts directly into money.

32
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:18,232
Seconds saved per checkpoint, times checkpoints per day, times GPUs per node, times what you pay per GPU-hour.

33
00:03:18,782 --> 00:03:26,966
At 128 gigabytes, that's roughly five dollars of avoided idle per checkpoint — before you multiply across the cluster.

34
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:40,048
So — if you run training jobs that checkpoint frequently, operate GPU infrastructure, or sell GPU capacity — AIFS turns storage speed into GPU efficiency.

35
00:03:40,598 --> 00:03:48,158
Try the pricing calculator to estimate your own savings — and find the prototype, the specs, and the benchmarks on GitHub.

36
00:03:48,658 --> 00:03:50,746
Stop paying the checkpoint tax.

